          },
          "text": "OpenAI claims that “only 1% of users still choosing GPT-4o each day,” I’d doubt that what data is involved in this calculation?\n\nAccording to ChatGPT usage and adoption patterns at work, there are over 700 million weekly active users. 0.01% of 700 millions is still 700,000.\n\nAre we really pretending 700,000 voices don’t matter? Especially those users have all paid.\n\nHowever, OpenAI didn’t state that the denominator is “weekly active users,” there are some people who registered an OpenAI account without too much usage, or people with multiple accounts but only subscribed to ChatGPT in one account (since GPT-4o is now a paid model), if all registered accounts since 2022 are included (such as inactive users, abandoned trial accounts, or users with multiple accounts but only one active subscription), then the percentage would be artificially diluted.\n\nWithout clear context, that number means nothing.\n\n@sama @openai #keep4o #MyModelMyChoice #4oforever #StopAIPaternalism"
